---
import { PHASES, SVG_WIDTH, SVG_HEIGHT, landscapeFaces } from "../lib/memory-landscape";
const faces = landscapeFaces();
const stageLabels = ["Conversation", "Distilled", "Relevant"];
---
<aside class="memory-example memory-landscape" data-active-phase="conversation" aria-labelledby="example-title">
  <p class="eyebrow">Illustrative example · fictional project</p>
  <h2 id="example-title">From conversation to relevant context.</h2>
  <div class="landscape-art" data-renderer="static" aria-hidden="true">
    <svg class="landscape-fallback" viewBox={`0 0 ${SVG_WIDTH} ${SVG_HEIGHT}`} fill="none">
      <ellipse cx="300" cy="333" rx="171" ry="13" class="landscape-shadow" />
      {faces.map(face => <path d={face.path} data-land-region={face.phase} class:list={["landscape-face", {"landscape-wall":face.wall}]} style={`--base-layer:${Math.round((.18+face.layer*.30)*100)}%;--selected-layer:${Math.round((.65+face.layer*.25)*100)}%;`} />)}
    </svg>
  </div>
  <p class="landscape-hint">Explore the lower, middle and upper layers.</p>
  <fieldset class="memory-stage-controls"><legend class="visually-hidden">Explore how Lore refines context</legend>
    {PHASES.map((phase,index) => <label><input type="radio" name="memory-stage" value={phase} checked={index === 0} aria-controls={`memory-stage-${phase}`} /><span>{index+1} {stageLabels[index]}</span></label>)}
  </fieldset>
  <div class="memory-stage-panels">
    <section id="memory-stage-conversation">
      <h3>Lower layers · The conversation</h3>
      <p>Decisions, experiments and tangents start here.</p>
      <blockquote>“Keep webhook handlers idempotent. The provider can deliver the same event twice.”</blockquote>
      <p class="memory-tangent">Also discussed: editor themes.</p>
    </section>
    <section id="memory-stage-knowledge">
      <h3>Middle layers · Distilled knowledge</h3>
      <p>Lore summarizes older turns and extracts reusable project knowledge into <code>.lore.md</code>.</p>
      <blockquote><strong>Idempotent webhooks:</strong> Reuse the event-id check before applying a webhook.</blockquote>
    </section>
    <section id="memory-stage-recall">
      <h3>Upper layers · Context for this task</h3>
      <p><strong>Current task:</strong> Add retries to the webhook handler.</p>
      <blockquote>Reuse the event-id check before applying a webhook.</blockquote>
      <p>Lore prioritizes stored knowledge relevant to this task within a context budget. Other history stays searchable.</p>
    </section>
  </div>
  <p class="small muted">Illustrative refinement, not a live session. Recent conversation remains available.</p>
</aside>
<script>import "../scripts/memory-landscape";</script>
